# --- Don't Get Phished — environment configuration ---
#
# Don't Get Phished is a hosted service. In production it runs on Supabase
# (Postgres + Auth + email). For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT and CI you can leave every
# Supabase var unset — the app automatically falls back to a zero-dependency
# file-backed store (./.data/izd-db.json) and a dev magic-link, so it builds,
# tests, and runs with no external services.

# --- Supabase (production backend) ---
# From your Supabase project: Settings → API. When both public vars are present,
# the app uses Supabase for the database AND for email-based auth.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only. Never exposed to the browser. Required for the Supabase datastore.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Local dev / CI fallback (only used when Supabase is NOT configured) ---
# Signing secret for the dev session cookie + magic tokens. The server hard-fails
# in production if the dev auth is active without a strong value here.
# AUTH_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Where the dev file store writes.
# DATA_FILE=./.data/izd-db.json
# Return the dev login code in the API response (no mail provider needed locally).
# Leave unset in dev; set to 1 only if you wire your own sender.
# EMAIL_ENABLED=1

# --- Optional ---
# Force a driver regardless of the above (mainly for testing): "supabase" | "json".
# DATABASE_DRIVER=json
# Redis for multi-instance matchmaking/presence/rate-limiting (not required for a
# single instance).
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
